#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""remote-term gateway administration: per-host keys, report tokens, pinned host keys, tunnels.

Run as root on the gateway. Easiest: `remote-term-admin join fa` prints one command to
paste on fa; once fa has run it and enrolled, `sync` (run automatically) pins its keys and
starts its web terminal. Manual order, if you prefer:
  remote-term-admin keygen fa          # print the line to put in ops' authorized_keys on fa
  remote-term-admin token fa           # print fa's report token (shown once)
  remote-term-admin hostkey fa ssh-ed25519 AAAA...   # pin fa's SSH host key
  remote-term-admin enable fa          # test SSH, then start fa's web terminal
"""

